P0-P2: MESHWEAVE research platform, control plane, planner, and runtime

Implements the MESHWEAVE distributed AI compute fabric through P2, plus the
planner and pipeline runtime from P4 and the EXP-010/EXP-011 harnesses.

Control plane (P1)
- Coordinator: FastAPI with node registration, heartbeat, live registry,
  topology ingest, planning, and workload endpoints
- Agent: real NVML telemetry (raises rather than inventing devices),
  closed control API, heartbeat loop, serve loop
- Wire transport: TLS framing, node certificates, workload-scoped HMAC tokens

Topology (P2)
- Network benchmark: RTT, jitter, loss, single/multi-stream TCP, sustained
  throughput, stability, UDP; N x N directed matrix (8 nodes -> 56 probes)
- Topology engine classifies links from measurement, gates tensor
  parallelism behind a datacenter check

Planning (P7)
- Execution Intelligence: deterministic cost-based planner answering the nine
  questions, including when the answer is "use one GPU"
- Cost model reporting dollars per million output tokens, with explicit
  unknown-cost handling rather than a guessed price
- Crossover detection for when adding nodes stops being economically useful

Runtime (P4)
- Qwen2.5 adapter with memory arithmetic validated against published configs
- Partitioner that refuses impossible configurations and states the deficit
- Activation transport with binary framing and per-hop instrumentation
- Pipeline runtime with preflight latency probing

Honesty guarantees (tested, not documented)
- Simulation is a separate module; experiments importing it fail a static test
- Report validator rejects benchmarks missing failures, cost, or evidence
- 44 tests pass; ruff clean; mypy --strict clean over 42 files

No GPU has been rented. Experiments that require hardware are present and
blocked with the exact command that will run them.